00:03:57,580 --> 00:04:00,420
For example, you got SQL-based databases

95
00:04:00,645 --> 00:04:03,502
like MySQL, or MySQL to be precise.

96
00:04:04,161 --> 00:04:07,773
MySQL is a very popular SQL database, and

97
00:04:07,773 --> 00:04:11,112
SQL in general, no matter if you use MySQL

98
00:04:11,385 --> 00:04:13,215
or another interpretation of it,

99
00:04:13,874 --> 00:04:16,892
is a relational database engine. So it's all

100
00:04:17,020 --> 00:04:19,766
about storing data and relations between

101
00:04:19,814 --> 00:04:23,651
data. SQL and MySQL is very popular, and you

102
00:04:23,667 --> 00:04:27,858
can absolutely use Deno with MySQL or with

103
00:04:27,938 --> 00:04:29,994
